      "text": "Solution: Observing the given information, the number of cans in each row that forms an arithmetic sequence. Since \\( a_n = a_1 + (n - 1)d \\), the number of cans in Row \\( n \\) is \\( 1 + (n - 1)2 = 2n - 1 \\).\n\nThe last term in the sequence is also given as \\( 100 \\):\n\\[ 2n - 1 = 100 \\]\nSolving for \\( n \\):\n\\[ 2n = 101 \\]\n\\[ n = \\frac{101}{2} \\]\nSince \\( n \\) must be an integer, and we know \\( n \\) must be odd, we can conclude that \\( n = 51.5 \\), but since \\( n \\) must be an integer, we round down to 51.\n\nTherefore, the number of rows in the display is \\( \\boxed{51} \\).",
