      "text": "Given the pattern, each row increases by two can spaces from the row above.\n\nLet $n$ repere the number of rows in the arrangement.\n\nIf the top row in this arrangement has 1 can, then the $2$ can row has $1+2=3$ cans.\nThe $4$ can row has $3+2=5$ cans.\nAnd the $2n$ can row has $2n+1$ cans.\nThe sum of all can in the arrangement the $n$-th row is given by:\n\n$$\\text{Sum} = n \\cdot (1 - n + 2n + 1) / 2 = n(n+2)/2$$\n\nSince the grocer arranged 100 cans since 100 = n(n+2)/2, it is equal to 50 cans.\n\n$$50 = n(n+2) / 2$$\n$$100 = n(n+2)$$\n\nThe equation can be rewritten by grouping:\n\n$$(n+1)^2 = 11^2$$\n\nSo, with $n = 5$, we have 5 rows that contains 100 cans.\n\nCorrect Answer: $\\boxed{5}$",
